# DTF tier manifest: maven-upload-tx-and-quality-s3  (artifact-keeper#3587, #3814, #3736; fixed in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: storage.s3 (MinIO; STORAGE_BACKEND=s3 for every repository).
#
# THE BUGS
#   #3587/#3814 the Maven hosted upload wrote the artifact row (an ON CONFLICT
#               upsert) and its artifact_metadata row as two autocommit
#               statements, so a metadata write that failed after the row
#               landed left a live artifact with no Maven metadata, and a
#               concurrent republish could observe the row before its
#               metadata existed. Fixed: both commit in one transaction.
#   #3736       quality checks (the automatic check and
#               POST /api/v1/quality/checks/trigger) read the artifact from the
#               default filesystem backend, so a check of anything in object
#               storage failed with "Storage key not found" and recorded no
#               result. Fixed: checks read from the repository's backend.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   #3814: the oracle installs a BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE trigger on
#   artifact_metadata (through the postgres container) that raises for one
#   artifactId only, PUTs that artifact, inspects the artifacts table, then
#   drops the trigger and retries. The rest of the database is untouched.
#   #3736: a Maven jar in the S3-backed repository, the trigger API, and the
#   quality_check_results table plus GET /api/v1/quality/checks.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)     #3587/#3814: with the metadata write failing, the upload is not
#             reported as a success and no live artifacts row remains for
#             the path; with the fault removed the retry leaves exactly one
#             row with its metadata. KNOWN-RED, recorded but not gated:
#             artifact-keeper#4837, the failed upload's bytes stay on the
#             repo-scoped S3 key and GET still serves them (200).
#             #3736: within 30 s of the trigger a new quality_check_results
#             row exists for the S3-stored artifact and GET /quality/checks
#             lists metadata_completeness=completed and nothing failed.
#             RED on 1.10.0.
#   (CONTROL) both images: a release jar uploads to S3, reads back byte-for-
#             byte, is listed in maven-metadata.xml and has its metadata row;
#             8 concurrent republishes of one SNAPSHOT path all answer 2xx and
#             leave exactly one live row, with metadata, serving one racer's
#             bytes (the #3587 500 is a 1.10.0 fix; the #3814 interleaving is
#             not reproducible from outside, so this is a control).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~30 authenticated calls, 8 of them concurrent.
PROFILES="storage.s3"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
